IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 3, Commencement of Acts (ss 3 to 6).
-- Sections 3 and 3A (the day and the moment an Act comes into operation) are in
-- au-interpretation-time.l4. This module has the rest: s 4 (powers exercised between
-- enactment and commencement) and s 6 (evidence of the date of assent). Sections 5 and
-- 5-numbered gaps are repealed (endnote 4).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Times are modelled as DAYS here: the text speaks of a
-- "start time", and the time of day inside the start day is not modelled in s 4.

§ `Part 3: Commencement of Acts`

§§ `Section 4: exercising a power between enactment and commencement`

-- 4(1) and (2): the section applies if an Act is enacted and, at a start time after its
-- enactment, the Act will confer power to make an appointment or an instrument of a
-- legislative or administrative character, because (a) the Act will commence at the
-- start time or (b) it will be amended at the start time by an enacted Act that commences
-- then. The power may then be exercised before the start time as if the relevant
-- commencement had occurred. 4(7): the same holds for a provision of an Act, so the
-- same function serves "an Act" and "a provision of an Act".
-- src:241 | 4 Exercise of powers between enactment and commencement of Act
-- src:242 | Application of section
-- src:243 | (1) This section applies if an Act is enacted and at a time (the start time) after its enactment the Act will confer power to make an appointment, or to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character (including rules, regulations or by-laws), because:
-- src:244 | (a) the Act will commence at the start time; or
-- src:245 | (b) the Act will be amended at the start time by an Act that has been enacted and that commences at that time.
-- src:246 | Exercise of power before start time
-- src:247 | (2) The power may be exercised before the start time as if the relevant commencement had occurred.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 4(1), (2) and (7) (src:241-247)
GIVEN `an Act is enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at a start time after enactment it will confer power to make an appointment or an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will commence at the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will be amended at the start time by an enacted Act that commences then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4 allows the power to be exercised before the start time` `an Act is enacted` `at a start time after enactment it will confer power to make an appointment or an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` `the Act will commence at the start time` `the Act will be amended at the start time by an enacted Act that commences then` MEANS
        `an Act is enacted`
    AND `at a start time after enactment it will confer power to make an appointment or an instrument of a legislative or administrative character`
    AND (   `the Act will commence at the start time`
         OR `the Act will be amended at the start time by an enacted Act that commences then`)

-- 4(4): the exercise of the power under 4(2) confers a power or right, or imposes an
-- obligation, before the relevant commencement only so far as is necessary or
-- convenient to (a) bring the appointment or instrument into effect, (b) bring the Act
-- conferring the power into operation, or (c) make that Act fully effective at or after
-- the start time.
-- src:249 | (4) The exercise of a power under subsection (2) does not confer a power or right or impose an obligation on a person before the relevant commencement except so far as is necessary or convenient for the purpose of:
-- src:250 | (a) bringing the appointment or instrument into effect; or
-- src:251 | (b) bringing the Act conferring power into operation; or
-- src:252 | (c) making the Act conferring power fully effective at or after the start time.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 4(4) (src:249-252)
GIVEN `it is necessary or convenient to bring the appointment or instrument into effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary or convenient to bring the Act conferring the power into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary or convenient to make the Act conferring the power fully effective at or after the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exercise may confer a power or right or impose an obligation before the relevant commencement` `it is necessary or convenient to bring the appointment or instrument into effect` `it is necessary or convenient to bring the Act conferring the power into operation` `it is necessary or convenient to make the Act conferring the power fully effective at or after the start time` MEANS
        `it is necessary or convenient to bring the appointment or instrument into effect`
     OR `it is necessary or convenient to bring the Act conferring the power into operation`
     OR `it is necessary or convenient to make the Act conferring the power fully effective at or after the start time`

-- 4(5): an appointment, or a provision of an instrument, made under 4(2) takes effect at
-- the start time or a later time specified in it. A time specified EARLIER than the start
-- time cannot make it take effect before the start time (4(4)).
-- src:253 | (5) An appointment, or a provision of an instrument, made under subsection (2) takes effect at the start time or a later time specified in the appointment or instrument.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 4(5) (src:253)
GIVEN `the start day` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the appointment or instrument, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day an appointment or instrument made before the start time takes effect` `the start day` `the day specified in the appointment or instrument, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day specified in the appointment or instrument, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the start day`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF specified GREATER THAN `the start day` THEN specified ELSE `the start day`

§§ `Section 6: evidence of the date of assent`

-- src:258 | 6 Evidence of date of assent
-- src:259 | The date appearing on the copy of an Act printed by the Government Printer, and purporting to be the date on which the Governor-General assented thereto, or made known the Sovereign’s assent, shall be evidence that such date was the date on which the Governor-General so assented or made known the Sovereign’s assent, and shall be judicially noticed.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 6 (src:258-259)
GIVEN `the date appears on a copy of the Act printed by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor-General assented or made known the Sovereign's assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed date is evidence of the date of assent, and is to be judicially noticed` `the date appears on a copy of the Act printed by the Government Printer` `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor-General assented or made known the Sovereign's assent` MEANS
    `the date appears on a copy of the Act printed by the Government Printer`
    AND `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor-General assented or made known the Sovereign's assent`
